    "summaries": [
      {
        "action_date": "2025-07-17",
        "action_desc": "Introduced in House",
        "text": "<p><strong>Tailored Regulatory Updates for Supervisory Testing Act of 2025 or the TRUST Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill permits additional small insured depository institutions that are considered well-capitalized and well-managed (per their most recent examination) to qualify for less frequent examinations conducted by federal&nbsp;financial&nbsp;regulators.&nbsp;Specifically, the bill raises the maximum asset level that qualifies an institution for less frequent examinations from less than $3 billion to less than $6 billion.&nbsp;</p>",
        "update_date": "2026-05-07T18:34:25Z"
      }
    ]
  },
